# Bindings for the specific apps and web apps you use.
#
# bindings.conf sources ~/.config/hypr/bindings-personal.conf, and Hyprland
# treats a missing source as a config error, so that file has to exist.
# install.sh copies this template into place when it is not there yet.
#
# It is deliberately kept out of the repository: the rest of the snapshot
# describes the machine, while this file would describe its owner — which
# mail provider, which messengers, which accounts.
#
# Everything below is commented out. Uncomment what you want, or write your own;
# an entirely commented-out file is valid and simply adds no bindings.

# --- Applications ---
# omarchy-launch-or-focus raises the window if it is already open instead of
# starting a second copy; the first argument is a regex matched against the class.
# bindd = SUPER SHIFT, M, Music, exec, omarchy-launch-or-focus spotify
# bindd = SUPER SHIFT, G, Messenger, exec, omarchy-launch-or-focus ^signal$ "uwsm-app -- signal-desktop"
# bindd = SUPER SHIFT, O, Notes, exec, omarchy-launch-or-focus ^obsidian$ "uwsm-app -- obsidian"
# bindd = SUPER SHIFT, SLASH, Passwords, exec, uwsm-app -- 1password

# --- Web apps ---
# omarchy-launch-webapp opens the URL as a standalone window with its own icon.
# If the url contains #, type it as ## — Hyprland treats a single # as a comment.
# bindd = SUPER SHIFT, A, AI chat, exec, omarchy-launch-webapp "https://example.com"
# bindd = SUPER SHIFT, E, Email, exec, omarchy-launch-webapp "https://mail.example.com"
# bindd = SUPER SHIFT, C, Calendar, exec, omarchy-launch-webapp "https://calendar.example.com"
